  (fn-do + restore-properties _
    (param type TypeId)
    (param declared SyntaxId)
    ; Stores again the properties an initializer's arguments fill, and each property whose
    ; value reads one stored again, in the order the properties are declared. The rest have
    ; their values already. A lazy property whose value reads one stored again is stale: what
    ; it holds, if it was evaluated, was computed from what is replaced. It is evaluated again
    ; where a value stored again reads it, and is otherwise left as it is.
